1j2c|n|A contagious disease of fowls, characterized by hoarseness, discharge from the nostrils and eyes, and an accumulation of mucus in the mouth, forming a "scale" on the tongue. By some the term pip is restricted to this last symptom, the disease being called roup by them. ; A seed, as of an apple or orange. ; One of the conventional figures or "spots" on playing cards, dominoes, etc.	a:1ixh,45,2;1euv,14,4;2u8,7,1~1euv,14,4;1ixh,45,2;2u8,7,1	v:ds5,32,6;132p,18,2;1a9l,11,2;a82,9,5;okc,3,3~ds5,32,6;a82,9,5;okc,3,3;132p,18,2;1a9l,11,2	V:ds5,30,5;d3o,10,5~d3o,10,5;ds5,30,5	n:1ixh,35,1;h0d,33,3;1pr8,12,6;132p,8,1~1pr8,12,6;h0d,33,3;132p,8,1;1ixh,35,1	N:t9y,32,21;e9e,11,3~t9y,32,21;e9e,11,3
