1j2g|v|To play on a pipe, fife, flute, or other tubular wind instrument of music. ; To call, convey orders, etc., by means of signals on a pipe or whistle carried by a boatswain. ; To emit or have a shrill sound like that of a pipe; to whistle. ; To become hollow in the process of solodifying; -- said of an ingot, as of steel. ; To perform, as a tune, by playing on a pipe, flute, fife, etc.; to utter in the shrill tone of a pipe. ; To call or direct, as a crew, by the boatswain's whistle. ; To furnish or equip with pipes; as, to pipe an engine, or a building.	o:2258,21,2~2258,21,2	s:2eq,15,1~2eq,15,1	D:20ry,11,3~20ry,11,3
